      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe this would create a circular dependency from java -\u003e tradefed/tests -\u003e java.\n\nMy cl allows the java -\u003e tradefed dep, then also creates the \n tradefed/tests -\u003e java,tradefed dependencies.  \nThis works because java doesn\u0027t depend on tradefed/tests.\n\nI\u0027m okay with moving test_module_config.go -\u003e java, since it seems to only work with `android_test` for now.  I think I might need a different rule for cc_test and sh_test.  I would leave the provider definition in tradefed, but move the module definition to java.\nOr we can leave it.\n\nI just went to this extreme to get it work to:\n  1) Ensure we only depend on Public parts or providers.\n  2) Unlock the achievement: \"can you make it work in tradefed\". from Joe\n\nLet me know where you want it to live.",
      "parentUuid": "2b4e2672_2305334f",
      "revId": "867ad74aabe4ae9fda97413f42a1adc17ad9bd3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
